      "round_summary": "Repair round 1/3: Fix assertion width-inference bug in `barrel_shifter_correct_rotation`. The expression `(inrReg >> io.amount) | (inrReg << (32.U - io.amount))` suffers from Chisel width inference: `32.U` is 6-bit wide, so `inrReg << (32.U - 0.U)` produces a 95-bit intermediate instead of 32 bits, causing a false assertion failure when amount=0. Fix: mask result with `(31, 0)` to truncate to 32 bits, matching the width of tmp5. The assertion label `barrel_shifter_correct_rotation` is preserved unchanged. No homologous assertions exist since the other two assertions (`spinner_progress`, `spin_feedback_active`) have different structure.",
